      "writtenOn": "2026-10-24T21:00:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have extra 128B in the buffer exactly because we want to avoid these types of ifs. Sure the processor is doing a fine job at predicting them, but if we force more rigor in the graph nodes, we have less branches and pretty sure everything will be just a tad faster. \n\nNodes, especially encapsulators, should always check if there\u0027s enough space left in the buffer as opposed to expecting the infra to police their behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "df93cba8_5315a31f",
      "revId": "f904c084e7734d009fa31e455fa76c5fec1d69ef",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
